`,e.jsxs(n.p,{children:["The ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://github.com/DLR-RM/BlenderProc/blob/76bd8b82ee19489843578ff045298642197bf883/docs/tutorials/renderer.md",children:"renderer tutorial"})," defines radial camera-to-point distance separately from camera-axis depth. The source requires an explicit antialiasing argument: ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://github.com/DLR-RM/BlenderProc/blob/76bd8b82ee19489843578ff045298642197bf883/blenderproc/python/renderer/RendererUtility.py#L260-L325",children:"non-AA depth"})," wires Blender's Depth pass to EXR; ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://github.com/DLR-RM/BlenderProc/blob/76bd8b82ee19489843578ff045298642197bf883/blenderproc/python/renderer/RendererUtility.py#L179-L256",children:"AA distance"})," uses linear Mist with a configurable maximum; AA depth delegates to that route and converts during loading. Record route and maximum, not only output key."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(n.p,{children:[e.jsx(n.strong,{children:"Source-visible calibration caveat:"})," ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://github.com/DLR-RM/BlenderProc/blob/76bd8b82ee19489843578ff045298642197bf883/blenderproc/python/postprocessing/PostProcessingUtility.py#L15-L75",children:"dist2depth/depth2dist"})," use only ",e.jsx(n.code,{children:"K[0,0]"})," for both pixel axes, although K import supports fx≠fy. This is an apparent non-square-intrinsics limitation requiring a later off-axis fixture, not a reproduced failure. Keep square-pixel calibration as the narrow initial condition; do not advertise arbitrary-intrinsics depth interchange from source review alone."]}),`
