`,e.jsxs(n.p,{children:[e.jsx(n.strong,{children:"Clip identity precedes tracking identity."})," ",e.jsx(n.code,{children:"init_state"})," loads frames, records one original height/width, and caches frame-zero features. ",e.jsx(n.code,{children:"reset_state"})," removes prompts, results, tracking metadata and object IDs, but retains images, dimensions, constants and cached features. ",e.jsx(n.strong,{children:"Inference:"})," changed renders, replacement frame files, changed crops or changed camera captures require a new state from the new immutable clip, not merely reset. A camera cut already inside the same clip is still image evidence; the predictor provides no authoritative scene/camera identity transition. ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://github.com/facebookresearch/sam2/blob/2b90b9f5ceec907a1c18123530e92e794ad901a4/sam2/sam2_video_predictor.py#L41-L153",children:"Initialization"})," · ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://github.com/facebookresearch/sam2/blob/2b90b9f5ceec907a1c18123530e92e794ad901a4/sam2/sam2_video_predictor.py#L675-L734",children:"reset/cache"})]}),`
`]}),`
`,e.jsxs(n.li,{children:[`
`,e.jsxs(n.p,{children:[e.jsx(n.strong,{children:"Frame index is not source time."})," JPEG names are filtered by extension and sorted by integer stem; state indexes their list positions. Missing filename numbers are not represented as missing temporal slots. MP4/bytes use Decord's frame iteration; the loader returns images and dimensions, not FPS/PTS. Both routes stretch frames to the model's square input and normalize RGB. ",e.jsx(n.strong,{children:"Adapter implication:"})," retain index → original filename/PTS/simulation tick plus crop/resize mapping; validate uniform dimensions rather than inferring time from index. ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://github.com/facebookresearch/sam2/blob/2b90b9f5ceec907a1c18123530e92e794ad901a4/sam2/utils/misc.py#L92-L309",children:"Loader"})]}),`
