`,e.jsx(n.p,{children:"Keep task set, action policy, model, permissions, scoring, and accepted engine mutations fixed. Cross two selection policies (global frame; crop plus global) with two retention policies (normal compacted context; explicit durable manifest plus evidence rehydration). Match visual/token budgets including rehydration and charge all selector/preprocessing/retry costs."}),`
`,e.jsx(n.p,{children:"First propose a deterministic mock bridge with numbered mutations and captures, delayed completion, cooperative and noncooperative cancellation, and original/derivative hashes. Script identical interruption locations: before dispatch; after engine acceptance before result; after result before compaction; after compaction before resume. Exercise default versus explicitly overridden nested signals, queued work, reload, and abandoned branches. These are proposed cases, not reproduced Pi bugs."}),`
`,e.jsx(n.p,{children:"Require separate assertions for duplicate mutations, wrongly assumed cancellation, stale connection use, branch contamination, missing evidence, original-to-derivative provenance, and final authoritative state. Count failures and unknown outcomes; do not score missing observations as success. A subsequent authorized project-owned engine fixture can test task quality with the same fault schedule. Freeze held-out cases before candidate selection."}),`
