`,e.jsxs(n.p,{children:[e.jsx(n.strong,{children:"Paper-described mechanism."})," A versioned hypothesis combines claim, investigation plan, decision criteria and alternatives. Selected investigations become Harbor packages while retaining those commitments. Replay diagnoses fixed-checkpoint failures; unrecorded alternatives require compatible restored-state execution. Matched development evaluation can retain the incumbent or accept model and harness changes separately or jointly. The reported life-science proposal-quality gains are preliminary: expert calibration remains pending, shared ancestry makes revision observations dependent, and retrospective literature correspondence does not establish causal influence or experimentally confirmed discoveries. ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://arxiv.org/html/2610.23839v1",children:"Paper v1, §§3.2–3.5, Appendices A.3–A.4, D–F"})]}),`
`,e.jsxs(n.p,{children:[e.jsx(n.strong,{children:"Released implementation boundary."})," At ",e.jsxs(n.a,{href:"https://github.com/Gen-Verse/DiscoveryRSI/tree/8f7214865548bc9b48170aa844e205341d24c4b9",children:["revision ",e.jsx(n.code,{children:"8f721486"})]}),", ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://github.com/Gen-Verse/DiscoveryRSI/blob/8f7214865548bc9b48170aa844e205341d24c4b9/src/discovery_rsi/core.py",children:e.jsx(n.code,{children:"core.py"})})," generates candidates, scores them, selects the maximum and stores selected episodes in JSONL; the no-candidate branch skips that append. Its ",e.jsx(n.code,{children:"ReplayBuffer"})," appends and reads records; it does not restore execution state. ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://github.com/Gen-Verse/DiscoveryRSI/blob/8f7214865548bc9b48170aa844e205341d24c4b9/src/discovery_rsi/harness.py",children:e.jsx(n.code,{children:"harness.py"})})," prompts for proposals and critiques. Its generation prompt passes the previous selected identifier, rather than the predecessor's claim and plan. ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://github.com/Gen-Verse/DiscoveryRSI/blob/8f7214865548bc9b48170aa844e205341d24c4b9/plugins/discovery-rsi/roles/role_compiler.md",children:e.jsx(n.code,{children:"role_compiler.md"})})," supplies instructions, not a Harbor package builder. No compiler, training pipeline or controlled harness-promotion implementation was identified in the ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://api.github.com/repos/Gen-Verse/DiscoveryRSI/git/trees/8f7214865548bc9b48170aa844e205341d24c4b9?recursive=1",children:"complete pinned tree"}),". Public source inspection therefore supports a portable proposal-loop scaffold, not reproduction of the full paper protocol."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(n.p,{children:[e.jsx(n.strong,{children:"Model and data availability."})," The ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://huggingface.co/Gen-Verse/DiscoveryRSI-27B/tree/main",children:"27B files listing"}),", observed at ",e.jsx(n.code,{children:"bf91ea68d49fe162c490f5ece38772fefd1de2d6"}),", contains only README and Git attributes; weights, tokenizer and configuration were absent. The ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://huggingface.co/Gen-Verse/DiscoveryRSI-27B",children:"model card"})," anticipates future checkpoint publication and leaves model/base/data terms to that release, despite the code README's released-checkpoint language. Separately, ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://huggingface.co/datasets/Gen-Verse/DiscoveryRSI-Hypothesis-Task-Examples",children:"three task examples"}),", observed at ",e.jsx(n.code,{children:"05d6044bd649a0e25bb3b58b0fbb582adb66b327"}),", expose instructions, verifiers, provenance, input requirements and a package ZIP. Their fixture/readiness success fields coexist with ",e.jsx(n.code,{children:"scientific_result: not_established"}),". This is example-artifact availability, not the training corpus or verified scientific execution. Project-owned ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://github.com/Gen-Verse/DiscoveryRSI/blob/8f7214865548bc9b48170aa844e205341d24c4b9/LICENSE",children:"code licensing"})," declares Apache-2.0; it does not license an absent checkpoint."]}),`
